   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# ML-05 — Feature Vector and Leakage/Privacy Check\n\nThis skeleton is yours to fill. Work the sections **in order** — each one has a one-line hint. Simple words, honest numbers."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## Setup & Data Loading"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os, sys, subprocess\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "IN_COLAB = \"google.colab\" in sys.modules\n",
    "REPO_URL = \"https://github.com/ABK998/flyrank-ML\"\n",
    "REPO_DIR = \"flyrank-ML\"\n",
    "\n",
    "if IN_COLAB:\n",
    "    if not os.path.isdir(REPO_DIR):\n",
    "        subprocess.run([\"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth\", \"1\", REPO_URL, REPO_DIR], check=True)\n",
    "    os.chdir(REPO_DIR)\n",
    "    subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"-q\", \"-r\", \"requirements.txt\"], check=True)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    while not os.path.isdir(\"data/raw\") and os.getcwd() != \"/\":\n",
    "        os.chdir(\"..\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(\"data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv\")\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded {len(df):,} rows from starter data. Working directory: {os.getcwd()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 1. Build the feature vector\n\n*Code that actually builds it — engineered features, categorical handling, fills.*"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "We build our clean feature matrix by selecting pre-decision behavioral and structural attributes, filling missing values safely, and engineering normalized scaling features."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Copy raw dataframe to build feature vector\n",
    "feat_df = df.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Handle missing values and fills\n",
    "feat_df[\"impressions_90d\"] = feat_df[\"impressions_90d\"].fillna(0)\n",
    "feat_df[\"content_age_days\"] = feat_df[\"content_age_days\"].fillna(feat_df[\"content_age_days\"].median())\n",
    "feat_df[\"avg_position\"] = feat_df[\"avg_position\"].fillna(100.0)\n",
    "feat_df[\"ctr\"] = feat_df[\"ctr\"].fillna(0.0)\n",
    "feat_df[\"word_count\"] = feat_df[\"word_count\"].fillna(feat_df[\"word_count\"].median())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Engineered features\n",
    "max_imp = feat_df[\"impressions_90d\"].quantile(0.95)\n",
    "feat_df[\"norm_impressions\"] = (feat_df[\"impressions_90d\"].clip(0, max_imp)) / max_imp\n",
    "\n",
    "max_age = feat_df[\"content_age_days\"].quantile(0.95)\n",
    "feat_df[\"norm_age\"] = (feat_df[\"content_age_days\"].clip(0, max_age)) / max_age\n",
    "\n",
    "selected_features = [\"norm_impressions\", \"norm_age\", \"avg_position\", \"ctr\", \"word_count\"]\n",
    "print(f\"Successfully built feature matrix with shape: {feat_df[selected_features].shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 2. Feature notes (meaning, missing, categorical, available-when?)\n\n*For each feature: what it means, how missing values are handled, and whether it exists BEFORE the moment you predict.*"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "- **impressions_90d**: Total search impressions over the past 90 days. Missing values filled with 0. Available prior to prediction moment.\n- **content_age_days**: Age of the content in days since publication/last update. Missing values filled with median age. Available prior to prediction moment.\n- **avg_position**: Average search engine ranking position. Missing values filled with 100.0 (representing deep unranked placement). Available prior to prediction moment.\n- **ctr**: Click-through rate over the observation window. Missing values filled with 0.0. Available prior to prediction moment.\n- **word_count**: Total word count of the document. Missing values filled with median word count. Available prior to prediction moment."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "feature_summary = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Feature\": [\"impressions_90d\", \"content_age_days\", \"avg_position\", \"ctr\", \"word_count\"],\n",
    "    \"Missing Count\": [df[\"impressions_90d\"].isna().sum(), df[\"content_age_days\"].isna().sum(), df[\"avg_position\"].isna().sum(), df[\"ctr\"].isna().sum(), df[\"word_count\"].isna().sum()],\n",
    "    \"Available Pre-Prediction\": [True, True, True, True, True]\n",
    "})\n",
    "print(feature_summary.to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 3. The leakage hunt\n\n*Attack your own features: label-derived columns, future windows, product flags. Show the test.*"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "We programmatically verify that target-derived columns, future performance windows, and internal product scores are absent from our feature set."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "forbidden_columns = [\"trend_direction\", \"trend_pct\", \"priority_score\", \"health_score\", \"future_clicks\"]\n",
    "active_features = [\"norm_impressions\", \"norm_age\", \"avg_position\", \"ctr\", \"word_count\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "for col in forbidden_columns:\n",
    "    assert col not in active_features, f\"LEAKAGE DETECTED: Forbidden column {col} is present in features!\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Leakage Hunt Passed: No target-derived or future-window columns exist in the active feature set.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 4. What I excluded and why\n\n*The list of fields you refused to use — with one line of why each.*"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "- **trend_direction**: Excluded because it is the target label itself.\n- **trend_pct**: Excluded because it represents a future-window percentage change leaking subsequent performance.\n- **priority_score**: Excluded because it is a proprietary downstream product rule, not a raw feature.\n- **health_score**: Excluded because it aggregates future health states that violate temporal prediction boundaries.\n- **client_id**: Excluded as a direct feature input to prevent memorizing specific client domains, though retained strictly for group-shuffled splitting."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "excluded_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Excluded Field\": [\"trend_direction\", \"trend_pct\", \"priority_score\", \"health_score\", \"client_id\"],\n",
    "    \"Reason for Exclusion\": [\n",
    "        \"Target label leakage\",\n",
    "        \"Future performance window leakage\",\n",
    "        \"Proprietary heuristic score\",\n",
    "        \"Future state aggregation\",\n",
    "        \"Pseudonymous ID reserved exclusively for group splitting\"\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "})\n",
    "print(excluded_df.to_string(index=False))"
   ]
